 Reflection's sharp your integral, 
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix}
\cos \theta + a & -\sin \theta \\
\sin \theta + b & \cos \theta
\end{vmatrix}
&= \cos^2 \theta - \sin^2 \theta - a \sin \theta - b \cos \theta + ab \\
&=1 + a b - a \sin \theta - b \cos \theta \\
&=1+(a b-\frac{b^2}{6})+\frac{ a^2}{6}+(ab-\frac{a^2}{6})-(a+b) \cos \theta \\
&= 1+ \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{6}+(ab-\frac{a^2}{6})+(ab-\frac{b^2}{6})-\cos \theta\left(a+b\right) \\
&=1+ \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{6}+(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right)-\cos \theta\left(a+b\right).
\end{align*}
Therefore, \begin{align*}
\left(1+ \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{6}+(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right)\right) &\leq 1 + \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{4}, \\
\left(\frac{ a^2}{6}+(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right) \right) & \leq \frac{ a^2}{4}.
\end{align*}
Hence,
\begin{align*}
1+ \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{6}+(ab-\frac{a^2}{6})+(ab-\frac{b^2}{6}) &= 1+ \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{6}+(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right)+2(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right) \\
&\geq 1+ \frac{\frac{6a^2}{4}+\frac{6b^2}{4}}{6} +\frac{\frac{6a^2}{4}+\frac{6b^2}{4}}{4}\\
&=\frac{a^2+b^2}{6}+(ab-\frac{a^2}{6})+(ab-\frac{b^2}{6}) \\
&=\frac{ a^2}{6}+(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right).
\end{align*}
Now,
\begin{align*}
1+ \frac{(a^2+b^2)}{6}+(ab-\frac{a^2}{6})+(ab-\frac{b^2}{6}) \geq \frac{ a^2}{6}+(a-\frac{b^2}{6})\left(b-\frac{a}{6}\right) \geq \frac{ a^2}{4},
\end{align*}
so the maximum value of $a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta$ in terms of $a$ and $b$ is 
$$\boxed{\left|\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\right| + \left|\frac{a-b}{2}\right|}.$$
</answer>

